OpenSCAD 98d891340e (the commit behind the 2026.04.03 snapshot),
CMakeLists.txt, the Emscripten section. Three changes:

1. CGAL_ALWAYS_ROUND_TO_NEAREST is added beside the
   CGAL_DISABLE_ROUNDING_MATH_CHECK that OpenSCAD already sets for
   Emscripten. WebAssembly can only round to nearest, so without it CGAL's
   interval arithmetic, which expects to set upward rounding, is unsound in
   the browser: minkowski() hulls fail CGAL assertions and fall back to a far
   slower method ("Minkowski failed").

2. -fexceptions becomes -fwasm-exceptions, where the file sets it for
   compiling and for linking, and -sDISABLE_EXCEPTION_CATCHING=0 goes: that
   setting belongs to Emscripten's JavaScript-based exceptions, and Emscripten
   refuses it beside -fwasm-exceptions. With WebAssembly's own exceptions no
   call that can throw goes through a JavaScript wrapper, so Chrome's
   JavaScript stack no longer limits how deep a model can recurse, and
   models render faster. The libraries the engine links were built the same
   way (see openscad-wasm-dc2ff913.patch).

3. -sNODEJS_CATCH_EXIT goes from the node build: the Emscripten this build
   uses (6.0.5) no longer supports it. The web build never set it.

Not in this file: the engine is linked with -sSTACK_SIZE=8388608 (8 MiB),
passed to CMake as -DCMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS by scripts/build-openscad-wasm.sh.
OpenSCAD's own recursion guard already assumes 8 MiB (STACKSIZE in this
file, used by src/platform/PlatformUtils.h), while Emscripten's default stack
is 64 KiB.

Made by applying the sed lines in scripts/build-openscad-wasm.sh to
upstream's file, then git diff. To apply it in an OpenSCAD checkout at
98d891340e: git apply openscad-98d89134.patch

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index cf09cb3..bdf262f 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -295,17 +295,16 @@ if (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL Emscripten)
   set(NULLGL ON CACHE BOOL "" FORCE)
   set(USE_MIMALLOC OFF CACHE BOOL "" FORCE)
   set(ENV{PKG_CONFIG_PATH} "/emsdk/upstream/emscripten/cache/sysroot/lib/pkgconfig")
-  target_compile_definitions(OpenSCADLibInternal PUBLIC CGAL_DISABLE_ROUNDING_MATH_CHECK)
+  target_compile_definitions(OpenSCADLibInternal PUBLIC CGAL_DISABLE_ROUNDING_MATH_CHECK CGAL_ALWAYS_ROUND_TO_NEAREST)
   target_link_libraries(OpenSCADLibInternal PUBLIC /emsdk/upstream/emscripten/cache/sysroot/lib/libz.a)
 
   # https://emscripten.org/docs/tools_reference/emcc.html
   # https://emscripten.org/docs/tools_reference/settings_reference.html
-  target_compile_options(OpenSCADLibInternal PUBLIC -fexceptions)
+  target_compile_options(OpenSCADLibInternal PUBLIC -fwasm-exceptions)
   target_link_options(OpenSCADExe PUBLIC
-    -fexceptions
+    -fwasm-exceptions
     -sABORT_ON_WASM_EXCEPTIONS
     -sALLOW_MEMORY_GROWTH=1
-    -sDISABLE_EXCEPTION_CATCHING=0
     -sEXIT_RUNTIME=1
     -sEXPORTED_RUNTIME_METHODS=['ENV','ERRNO_CODES','FS','PATH','callMain']
     -sMAXIMUM_MEMORY=4GB
@@ -324,7 +323,6 @@ if (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL Emscripten)
   elseif (WASM_BUILD_TYPE STREQUAL "node")
     target_link_options(OpenSCADExe PUBLIC
       -sENVIRONMENT=node,worker
-      -sNODEJS_CATCH_EXIT
       -sNODERAWFS
 
       # Single .js (more elegant for CLI release) is larger than separate .js & .wasm (preferred for web)
